  "answer": "Other users have reported this before: the Mouse Without Borders \"New Key\" button does nothing and no devices are listed. I found no ticket that matches your settings-window problem or the fix you applied, so those tickets cover only the New Key symptom. They suggest these steps, roughly in this order:\n1. In the PowerToys General tab, turn the Mouse Without Borders toggle off and on again (reported to work in #26995). Doing this from the MWB page itself does nothing.\n2. If the old standalone Mouse Without Borders is installed, uninstall it. One user could not generate a key until it was gone (#26995).\n3. Turn off \"Always run as administrator\" and restart PowerToys without admin rights. Generate a new key and connect your other devices. Then restart PowerToys on every machine and turn admin back on if you want it (#35904).\n4. Make sure every machine runs the same PowerToys version. In #35904, some users said the problem went away after updating or reverting to a different version.\n\nIf none of this helps, add your bug report ZIP and logs to one of those tickets. #35904 was closed as a duplicate of #35807."
 },
